# gh-image — the ONE pinned build bin/gh-attach will run. Parsed as data (never sourced).
#   version <tag>        the upstream tag, drogers0/gh-image (MIT)
#   commit  <sha>        the commit that tag points at when it was audited (2026-11-05)
#   url-base <https>     where the release binaries live; install-gh-image.sh refuses any other prefix
#   sha256 <os-arch> <hex>  checksum of the release binary `<os>-<arch>` (the default, kooky, build — not hbd-*)
# Changing a line here is a change of the security boundary: re-audit the new tag first
# (setup/briefs/gh-image-upload-tool.md, § Audit; docs/gh-attach.md).
# darwin-arm64 was downloaded and hashed by hand on 2026-11-05 and equals the release's checksums.txt;
# the other three rows are copied from that same checksums.txt (unverified by download).
